Enum is basically a custom data type, in which we will assign the constant value of the application in a block and refer that value as object in entire application.
Redux:
1. Redux is tiny library which is using to maintain the global state in the form of store and this state must be sharable with n number of applications 
(React/Angular/ simultaneously)
2. We can write redux application with consistent centralized debuggable state management.
3. Redux can be described in 3 fundamentals : 
	3.1 Single source of truth ( global state of application is stored in an Object tree within single store)
	3.2 State is always read only ( state is always be readable in redux which can be change only by pure function)
	3.3 Change are made by pure function ( state object tree is transformed by action in which reducer is called which is called the pure function 
		and return the changed or final state.)
	3.4 we can install the redux toolkit by the following command using npm bundler
			npm install @reduxjs/toolkit
			npm install react-redux
4.Using redux we always following flux architecture as mentioned below
	Action -> Dispatcher -> Store -> Reducer -> final return changed state which is accessible by react components.
5.Redux itself a separate container which is managing own lifecycle to maintain all the principles based on the implementation.

context Api is a mechanism in which state are managing in react level
redux is a tiny library maintaining in global level
now state can be shared in all application and maintain the state in application level

Deep drilling -  threads are created - lifecycle hook of component - thread is alive - effect - vd
